WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.550 line:1
Good to be with you from the White House tonight.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.790 line:1
I’m Tony Dokoupil.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.030 line:1
The breaking news right now.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:14.850 line:1
President Trump welcomes China’s Xi Jinping with a military flyover and a lavish state dinner.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.190 line:1
China’s first state visit in more than a decade.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.720 line:1
But some members of the President’s own party aren’t happy.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:29.420 line:1
When you have world leaders looking at this reception compared to the way President Zelenskyy has been received, you go, like, that’s a WTF moment.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:34.460 line:1
Also breaking tonight, the monster storm set to slam the East Coast.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.890 line:1
A powerful nor’easter.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:36.950 line:1
Winds up to 60 miles an hour.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.320 line:1
Heavy rain and flooding, as well.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.010 line:1
Rob Marciano in the storm zone.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:46.020 line:1
And why Stanford University is apologizing for a photo on a campus banner.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.940 line:1
What it shows and the backlash tonight.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.910 line:1
High-speed chase.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:58.260 line:1
A carjacking suspect races through streets near Miami evading police multiple times speeding in reverse.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.100 line:1
How it ended.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.800 line:1
CBS News exclusive.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.960 line:1
A sneak peek of Taylor Swift’s new video for the song "Patient Zero" before it drops at midnight.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.190 line:1
And panda diplomacy is back.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:15.630 line:1
Tonight, China’s new gift to America.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:23.460 line:1
This is the "CBS Evening News" with Tony Dokoupil, reporting tonight from the White House.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.320 line:1
And good evening.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:31.350 line:1
Great to have you with us on a historic Thursday night in Washington, D.C. you’ve got a view of the North Portico of the White House behind me.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:37.550 line:1
That is the entry point for tonight’s state dinner in the East Room, after what has already been a day of major events.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:49.820 line:1
President Trump welcoming Chinese President Xi Jinping to the White House, his first visit to Washington in more than a decade, a moment marked by flyovers of both U.S. fighter jets and a B-2 stealth bomber.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:57.950 line:1
Inside, President Trump hailing what he called a truly great friendship, while Xi, through a translator, told Trump "I am ready to work with you."

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.240 line:1
And our Weijia Jiang is here with me with more on that part of the story.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.640 line:1
Weijia, good evening.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:10.150 line:1
Tony, it’s great to have you here in Washington where that very delicate dance between the world’s superpowers is on full display.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:18.710 line:1
Presidents Trump and Xi Jinping are balancing their warm relationship with the fierce competition between the U.S. and China.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:27.580 line:1
President Trump hosted his Chinese counterpart, Xi Jinping for formal talks at the White House, praising a, quote truly great friendship.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:36.440 line:1
But they are grappling with several thorny issues: Iran, Taiwan, trade, and the intense AI arms race.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.580 line:1
AI leaders are urging the U.S. and China to implement global guidelines.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:44.610 line:1
Trump recently said "I want to leave it exactly where it is."

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.970 line:1
We don’t want to restrict them where all of a sudden we come in second to China.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:56.740 line:1
Xi said both the U.S. and China have the capability and responsibility to develop and manage AI for good.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:06.300 line:1
Trump put on a show for the Chinese leader, with a tour of Marine One, a flyover, and a performance by a military band.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:15.400 line:1
Back in 2012, private citizen Trump criticized then-president Obama for doing similar, calling it "so wrong" to give Xi a full honor ceremony.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:22.070 line:1
The high-profile visit comes as the administration faces a court fight over press access.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:34.010 line:1
Today, a federal judge ordered the White House to immediately reinstate press credentials for CNN, MS NOW, and "Politico," after Trump banned them over what he called negative coverage.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.640 line:1
But the case is not closed.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.850 line:1
This is not a final ruling on the merits.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:46.300 line:1
This does not mean that CNN and MS NOW and "Politico" won.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:04:04.200 line:1
Even though journalists from those outlets are back on White House grounds for now, the administration has not restored CNN as part of the press pool that provides TV coverage of the President, and until that happens, the other networks will not participate which is why we didn’t have footage today, Tony, of all of those events.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.680 line:1
Yeah, a big gap there.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.850 line:1
Speaking of TV, there is a new pro-Trump ad airing on cable and broadcast that apparently has tax dollars mixed up in it.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.670 line:1
What do we know?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:35.710 line:1
That’s right, so this ad features the President talking about defeating communism, and it’s mostly, you know, a promotion of his achievements, but it’s the words "paid for by the U.S. government" that is drawing fire because some Democrats say the ad violates federal ethics rules that prohibit the use of government resources for campaign purposes.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:42.830 line:1
But the White House says it’s quote, clearly not political and a similar ad will air on this network tonight, Tony.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:46.680 line:1
Weijia, thank you very much, it is great to be here with you in Washington.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:55.610 line:1
And earlier on Capitol Hill, I spoke with Senator Thom Tillis of North Carolina, one of the Republicans trying to make sense of the President’s shift toward China between his first and his second terms.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.870 line:1
He says he just can’t figure it out.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:03.130 line:1
How do you feel about the state visit and the state dinner tonight?

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:03.910 line:1
Do you agree with the timing?

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.200 line:1
I actually think it’s bad timing.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:14.400 line:1
I mean, we are at a time where President Trump, who I support a majority of the time, you know ran on a campaign of holding China accountable.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.880 line:1
I’m worried about the trend of spending more time with despots and less time with Democratic leaders of nations.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.590 line:1
So you agree the President has taken a softer approach toward China in his second term?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:32.680 line:1
Look, I mean, this President in a speech in this term took on the Chinese for degrading and stealing voter data.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:41.070 line:1
Whatever has changed had to have been at a confidential level because I haven’t seen any public basis for the sea change that we see right now in our posture towards China.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.710 line:1
You’ve got to have a relationship with them, I get that.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:54.800 line:1
But when you have world leaders looking at this reception compared to the way, maybe President Zelenskyy has been received, you go, like, it’s a WTF moment.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:13.820 line:1
Tillis is leaving Congress in January after a series of differences with President Trump, and he is one of four Republican senators who just yesterday called on the Trump administration to deliver on a stalled $14 billion arms deal for Taiwan -- a deal of course, that China opposes.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:25.230 line:1
Meanwhile, back in New York at the U.N. General Assembly today Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu mounted a campaign-style defense of Israel’s battles in the Middle East -- and took on New York’s Mayor in the process.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:29.700 line:1
He called accusations of genocide in Gaza, quote, the biggest lie of the century.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:35.530 line:1
He labeled the dozens of delegates who walked out before he even began to speak moral cowards.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:43.010 line:1
And he accused Mayor Mamdani who has repeatedly said Netanyahu should be arrested over alleged war crimes, of trying to silence him.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:48.050 line:1
Netanyahu also had a message for the leaders of Iran as that war drags on.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:55.160 line:1
One day, and it may not be far away, the Iranian people will be free.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:07:02.560 line:1
Their murderous regime will be toppled by its lies, by its corruption, by its cruelty.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:09.860 line:1
Outside the speech dozens of antiwar protesters blocked a road and were arrested, among them the actor Susan Sarandon.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:14.180 line:1
And we turn now to weather and the powerful nor’easter bearing down on the Atlantic Coast.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:18.840 line:1
Warnings of high surf, strong winds and heavy rain are posted for hundreds of miles.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:23.190 line:1
Our Tom Hanson has it all covered tonight from Massachusetts.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:27.610 line:1
This powerful nor’easter punished several states today.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:30.640 line:1
Starting with North Carolina’s Outer Banks.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:36.580 line:1
Surging water washed out the main highway connecting these popular barrier islands.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:45.310 line:1
The pounding surf quickly consumed streets and surrounded homes, with waves topping 16 feet and wind gusts of more than 45 miles per hour.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:52.040 line:1
In Virginia, the high winds pushed massive amounts of water into its low-lying tidal basin flooding communities in the Norfolk area.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.780 line:1
It’s very scary.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.850 line:1
This area can really be, it can be devastating.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:04.530 line:1
Parts of New Jersey’s coastline are already showing signs of beach erosion, a major concern in these potent storms.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:07.010 line:1
In the coastal town of Sea Bright, locals were on high alert.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.930 line:1
So we are, like, preparing for it to flood pretty bad.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:22.680 line:1
Meanwhile meanwhile Hurricane Polo, one of the strongest storms ever in the Pacific, regained strength off Mexico’s southwestern coast sending heavy bands of rain and huge waves crashing ashore.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.320 line:1
As weather-weary residents in southern California hoped for the best.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:32.210 line:1
Hurricane Marie left us with a lot less sand than we started with, and so our guys are just shoring up our defenses.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:47.100 line:1
While mainland North America is seeing the impacts from these two separate storms, hundreds of miles away Hawaii residents brace for Tropical Storm Nolo, expected to gain Hurricane strength bringing as much as 35 inches of rainfall to the same areas battered by Hurricane Lala.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.330 line:1
It can get very serious very fast.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.450 line:1
And Tony, take a look behind me, you can see the waves are rolling in.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:56.610 line:1
That is only going to intensify as we head into the weekend.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:01.350 line:1
Now, at the height of the storm waves could reach up to 25 feet Tony.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.590 line:1
All right, Tom thank you very much.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:06.270 line:1
On that note, let’s get the forecast now from meteorologist Rob Marciano.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.200 line:1
He is tracking the nor’easter as well as a swarm of hurricanes out there in the Pacific.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:12.730 line:1
Rob, good evening.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.280 line:1
Hey, Tony.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.240 line:1
Yeah, lots to get to, so let’s get to what’s happening here in the Northeast.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.530 line:1
The coastal advisories.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:26.470 line:1
The high wind warning now that was just posted for Eastern New England, including Boston and Providence, and the major flooding that’s possible across the coastlines there.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.330 line:1
Beach erosion, we mentioned that.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.430 line:1
And the winds could be over 60 miles per hour and the big waves.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:51.980 line:1
So let’s go with one of our computer models, the most reliable one shows a low just off the coast of the Carolinas and then it drifts slowly off towards the north and maybe towards the west, closer to the Jersey Shore, so that’s when we will start to get impacts in New Jersey, New York, and then Connecticut, as well, and then kind of filling out and drifting Northeast on Sunday, and weakening as it does so, but it will be a high impact weekend for sure, with rainfall.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.340 line:1
Into the Pacific we go.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:59.940 line:1
Polo still a major Hurricane expected to make landfall in the Baja as a cat 2, but Nolo is of more immediate concern.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:11.680 line:1
About 300 miles south of the Big Island of Hawaii, likely to make an approach there as a major storm, and like Lala did just about a month ago, so big time rains there as they still recover from that storm.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.060 line:1
So high anxiety in Hawaii and the Northeast over the next couple of days.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:15.590 line:1
Tony?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.100 line:1
All right, Rob thank you very much.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:25.830 line:1
In other news, into Pittsburgh now, the story of a prominent doctor stabbed to death in his own home, attacked in the middle of the night while he and his wife were sleeping.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.830 line:1
The details now from CBS’s Meg Oliver.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.320 line:1
Multiple people stabbed.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:34.850 line:1
A horrible scene unfolded shortly after midnight.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:38.800 line:1
Police say 32-year-old Elijah Hemingway broke into the home of Dr.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:39.910 line:1
Idris Evans and his home of Dr.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:46.280 line:1
Idris Evans and his wife near Pittsburgh and stabbed the pair multiple times while they were sleeping.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.980 line:1
It was a very violent scene.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.240 line:1
The bedroom furniture broken mirrors broken.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.180 line:1
It was a very, it was a very graphic scene.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:03.110 line:1
Police say Evans’ wife managed to escape and ran from their home with their two young children.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:07.650 line:1
The couple was taken to the hospital in critical condition but Evans later died.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:11.380 line:1
We do not know if there was any preexisting relationship.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.770 line:1
The woman did not know this male.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:20.190 line:1
We are trying to determine if the two males knew each other.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:27.010 line:1
According to the police report, his wife said the suspect was in his underwear and remembers her husband addressing the attacker as "Elijah."

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.140 line:1
However, she said she did not know the man.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:33.610 line:1
Investigators say the suspect was found hiding behind a nearby home.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.690 line:1
He was hiding.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:48.470 line:1
There was an area of my garden it’s not particularly well manicured like the other parts and he had found a way to conceal himself, but apparently he was injured and bleeding.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:53.470 line:1
Police say there is no motive at this time, but that Hemingway has an extensive criminal background.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:57.550 line:1
He now faces multiple charges including homicide.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:11:58.650 line:1
Tony?

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.750 line:1
Meg, thank you.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:09.100 line:1
Stanford University is apologizing tonight for what it calls a serious error in judgment, editing a photo of students to alter looks, race and gender.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:14.100 line:1
And as our Jonathan Vigliotti reports, one of the students was transformed beyond recognition.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:19.560 line:1
A Stanford University photographer took this picture to promote the student dining services.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:21.830 line:1
Races.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:27.170 line:1
Because last week, Stanford used AI to change the image to this.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:31.000 line:1
When compared side by side, the Latino man became a black woman.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.970 line:1
The other two faces were altered.

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:44.220 line:1
The student who disappeared from the photo, Billy Ramirez, told "the Stanford Daily," "seeing my identity changed and being left out of the picture made me feel in a way, silenced and erased."

00:12:44.220 --> 00:13:03.060 line:1
The other two students posted a letter to the Stanford community on Substack demanding a public apology and writing, "using AI to create so-called diversity rather than showing true Stanford diversity, is a clear sign of the administration slapping a band-aid on a greater DEI problem."

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:13.420 line:1
Stanford University figures show that in recent years, black and Latino enrollment have sharply declined since the Supreme Court’s 2023 ruling banning race-based admissions.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:18.120 line:1
Today, Stanford said the photo manipulation was in violation of University policy.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:24.860 line:1
Both the alteration and lack of disclosure in this case violate that policy.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.350 line:1
And that photo was part of a banner welcoming students back to campus.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:34.540 line:1
It has since been taken down but it’s still unclear, Tony why it was doctored in the first place.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.520 line:1
Jonathan, thank you very much.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:43.510 line:1
We also have more tonight on the death of those two Mississippi college students and the possible link to a widely-available drug.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:49.850 line:1
Our Lilia Luciano now with what we are learning and the new warning from authorities.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.140 line:1
Possible OD, they do not believe the subject is breathing.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:14:01.820 line:1
State authorities are working to expedite toxicology reports for two University of Mississippi students who were found dead on Monday in separate incidents.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.960 line:1
We are not even sure that both of them were overdose.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:17.410 line:1
Investigators say there is no evidence the deaths are connected, but acknowledged that similarly-packaged kratom a popular supplement that can produce an opioid-like effect was found at both scenes.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:18.210 line:1
In what form was the kratom?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.680 line:1
It appears it is very similar.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:29.520 line:1
We are concerned it is coming from a common source and if it did result in the death of these two young individuals, we will want to make sure they are identified at the source.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:47.330 line:1
Today, the University of Mississippi identified the two students as 18-year-old Aidan Hamilton a freshman from Englewood Colorado, found unresponsive in a dorm and 20-year-old Robert Strang, a junior from Atlanta, who authorities say was found in an off-campus apartment.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:55.720 line:1
A spokesperson for the Strang family said in a statement that they are trying to process this unimaginable loss.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.560 line:1
Students on campus expressed grief, shock, and fear over the deaths.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:06.030 line:1
I think for several students this has made them too upset to go to classes.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:14.320 line:1
And that toxicology report that could confirm whether any substances played a role in either of the deaths could come out as early as tomorrow.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:14.880 line:1
Tony?

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:17.480 line:1
Lilia, thank you very much.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:29.960 line:1
Still ahead on the broadcast tonight, a police chase that started at the hospital and ended at the jail.

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:36.580 line:1
In Miami-Dade County today, police say a man broke himself out of a hospital carjacked a woman, and then led authorities on a wild chase.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.560 line:1
Our Cristian Benavides has details.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:50.910 line:1
A wild scene playing out in South Florida as the man behind the wheel of this black Nissan led police on a chase through the streets of northwest Miami-Dade County.

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:54.290 line:1
Police have tried on several occasions to use P.I.T. maneuvers.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:16:05.930 line:1
Hialeah police say Eugene Jordan Brown sped through several residential neighborhoods as Miami-Dade County sheriff’s deputies and Florida Highway Patrol tried several times unsuccessfully to P.I.T. maneuver the vehicle.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:09.670 line:1
At one point, Brown puts the vehicle in reverse to evade officers.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:13.540 line:1
He then speeds away, nearly striking police vehicles and other drivers.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:17.040 line:1
Get him!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:26.730 line:1
Police say the driver may have been receiving mental health treatment at a local hospital, where the suspect carjacked a woman getting out of her vehicle and forced himself in.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:33.000 line:1
This may finally be the moment where police have brought this vehicle down.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:39.940 line:1
After several attempts and about 30 minutes of giving chase, police were finally able to stop the driver.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:46.400 line:1
They surrounded the vehicle with guns drawn, pulled the suspect from the window, and took him the chase played out on live television.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:50.840 line:1
Authorities say that the woman who was carjacked had to be taken to the hospital for treatment.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:51.680 line:1
Tony?

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:54.240 line:1
Cristian, thank you very much.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:17:01.430 line:1
After the break, the delivery guy, the rooster, and what happened next.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:14.770 line:1
Some Americans on vacation in Alberta, Canada, say they saw a moose, some elk, and this unbelievable landing, a small plane coming in steep and leveling off and touching down safely on the side of a highway there.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:16.610 line:1
They got the video to prove it.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:20.130 line:1
That’s a pretty beautiful backdrop there, as well.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:24.260 line:1
And spare a thought for your local delivery people.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.910 line:1
[Rooster crowing] ooh-ee!

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:36.350 line:1
[Rooster crowing] they see it all, and if you are this Amazon guy in South Carolina, that includes a not-so-friendly rooster blocking your path.

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:38.860 line:1
But fear not, all ye waiting on packages.

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:44.260 line:1
He took a shortcut right over the porch railing and back to his van.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:51.760 line:1
We have a peek tonight at Taylor Swift’s new music video.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:57.750 line:1
"CBS Mornings" shared this exclusive first look, a clip for "Patient Zero," Taylor’s new single.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:10.090 line:1
The song comes out tomorrow while the video with actors Dakota Johnson and Colin Farrell in it, will debut Sunday at the MTV Video Music Awards, airing right here on CBS.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:18.200 line:1
And when we come back tonight the U.S.-China relationship beyond the pomp and the pandas.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:27.840 line:1
We are back live from Washington, D.C. after a day of meetings President Trump is honoring President Xi Jinping of China with a state dinner in the East Room tonight.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:33.660 line:1
It includes a performance from President Trump’s favorite tenor, that’s Christopher Macchio.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:41.710 line:1
A three-course meal, also, of yellow squash, sesame-crusted sea bass, and a honey ice cream made from the White House’s own hives.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:51.450 line:1
There will be a toast of sparkling wine meant to honor the so-called toast of peace between Richard Nixon and the Chinese premier in 1972.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:57.580 line:1
And we learned today of another form of diplomacy that’s coming and this one’s a lot more accessible to the rest of us.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:01.010 line:1
President Xi announced a new gift of giant pandas.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:15.830 line:1
They are on their way to a zoo in Atlanta, part of what Xi called an envoy of friendship between our two nations, a gesture that dates all the way back to 1972, when First Lady Pat Nixon told the Chinese premier how much she enjoyed the pandas in Beijing.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:23.000 line:1
A pair of them then arrived in the U.S. the start of 50 years now of panda diplomacy.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:30.890 line:1
And yet, all the pandas in the world and a state dinner every night of the year wouldn’t be enough to hide the strain in this U.S.-China relationship.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:38.280 line:1
Tonight, they’re going to be in the same room, but still far apart on the biggest issues facing our two countries and the world.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:39.820 line:1
That’s another day in America.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:45.240 line:1
I’m Tony Dokoupil here in Washington, D.C. for all of us at CBS News thank you for watching.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.070 line:1
Good night.
